NAME
       systemd-analyze - show how long the system took to boot

SYNOPSIS
       systemd-analyze [time]
       systemd-analyze blame

DESCRIPTION
       systemd-analyze reports on the last boot. With no command (or time) it
       prints how long the kernel, the initial RAM disk and the rest of the
       start-up took, and when the default target was reached. blame lists
       units by the time they took to start, slowest first, which helps find
       what makes a boot slow.

EXAMPLES
           systemd-analyze
           systemd-analyze blame | head

NOTES
       A unit that takes long in blame is not always the problem: it may be
       waiting for another unit.

SEE ALSO
       systemctl(1), journalctl(1)
